# Linux-C.O.S -- tools Parrot ships that are NOT already covered by any
# kali-tools-* category (computed by diffing the two catalogs). Most of these
# are plain Debian packages; apt will only reach for parrot.org's repo
# (added in the hook below, at low pin priority) for the handful that aren't.
2ping
awscli
azure-cli
backdoor-factory
can-utils
device-pharmer
etherape
etherwake
libfreefare-bin
libnfc-bin
mfcuk
mfoc
mfterm
netcat-openbsd
node-aws4
ow-shell
ow-tools
proxychains
python3-shodan
rsync
scantool
smali
smartmontools
smbclient

# Removed after a real build attempt confirmed these 6 don't resolve from
# Parrot's current 'lory' repo under these names (renamed/dropped upstream,
# or parrot-meta-sdr specifically is itself a metapackage that isn't
# published as an installable .deb): convoc2, king-phisher, logseq,
# parrot-meta-sdr, rocket, rtlsdr-scanner.

# Also removed (Kali-rolling base, second real build attempt): afl, bluez-hcidump,
# gscanbus, pev, rclone, s3backer -- not resolvable by these names from
# Parrot's repo layered on Kali either (renamed/dropped/moved upstream).
# afl is superseded by aflplusplus anyway (already in kali-tools-vulnerability).
